    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_1582eb78",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The image shows a person's legs with tattoos, one of which is a seashell, covered in sand, with overlaid text claiming that if you put your ear to it, you can smell the ocean. This is a humorous, fictional claim that plays on the idea of tattoos having sensory properties. The overall intent is to create a lighthearted, absurd joke about tattoos and sensory perception, likely intended to amuse viewers. There is no toxicity present in the meme. The joke is based on a whimsical, non-harmful fantasy and does not target any specific group or individual with abuse, hate, or harmful stereotypes. The visual elements (tattoos, sand, beach setting) are used to support the textual joke via juxtaposition, creating a surreal and amusing scenario. The meme is not propagandistic, abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or harmful in any way.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_64ede9da"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
